    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d295">

                <pb facs="0390" n="224" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg224"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.811/280</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Reinsch to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-11-21T13:00:00+08:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 21, 1917, 1 p.m</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Carey requests the following in substance be communicated to Stone, President,
                    International Corporation. Your cable November 8, has been transmitted to
                    Government. Canal contract signed subject conditions named therein. However
                    Chinese Government requests <pb facs="0391" n="225" xml:id="pg225"/> not send
                    engineers until after my arrival New York. Morgan advised as to the above
                    telegram and his indorsement secured to contract.</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Carey.</hi>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Reinsch</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
